WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.817
HKDSE 2026, Paper 1, Question 3. This is the full worked solution in English.

2
00:00:08.237 --> 00:00:18.896
The coordinates of the points P and Q are (minus 6, 5) and (2, 1) respectively. P is translated downwards by r units to R.

3
00:00:19.056 --> 00:00:28.268
(a) Write down, in terms of r, the coordinates of R. (b) Find r such that angle PQR equals 90 to the power degrees.

4
00:00:28.688 --> 00:00:34.477
STEP 1 times TRANSLATION DOWNWARDS goes to PART (a).

5
00:00:34.637 --> 00:00:48.786
Key rule: Translation. (x, y) tends to (x, y-r) (down r units). The x minus coordinate stays minus 6, so R equals (minus 6, 5 minus r).

6
00:00:48.946 --> 00:00:59.656
A translation downwards by r units leaves the x minus coordinate unchanged and decreases the y minus coordinate by r: R equals (minus 6, 5 minus r).

7
00:01:00.076 --> 00:01:05.322
STEP 2 times COMPARE THE GRADIENTS AT Q.

8
00:01:05.482 --> 00:01:19.514
Key rule: Gradient of a Segment. m equals y sub 2 minus y sub 1 over x sub 2 minus x sub 1. QP rises 4 over a run of minus 8, so m sub QP equals minus 12.

9
00:01:19.674 --> 00:01:23.968
QR has the same run minus 8 and rise 4 minus r.

10
00:01:24.128 --> 00:01:33.611
angle PQR equals 90 to the power degrees means the segment QP and the segment QR are perpendicular, so the product of their gradients is minus 1.

11
00:01:33.771 --> 00:01:48.336
From Q(2, 1) to P(minus 6, 5) the x minus coordinate changes by x sub P minus x sub Q equals minus 6 minus 2 equals minus 8 and the y minus coordinate by y sub P minus y.

12
00:01:48.496 --> 00:01:52.566
sub Q equals 5 minus 1 equals 4.

13
00:01:52.726 --> 00:02:07.621
m sub QP equals y sub P minus y sub Q over x sub P minus x sub Q equals 5 minus 1 over minus 6 minus 2 equals 4 over minus 8 equals minus 12 From Q(2, 1) to R(minus 6.

14
00:02:07.781 --> 00:02:20.460
5 minus r) the changes are x sub R minus x sub Q equals minus 6 minus 2 equals minus 8 and y sub R minus y sub Q equals (5 minus r)-1 equals 4 minus r.

15
00:02:20.620 --> 00:02:28.746
m sub QR equals (5 minus r)-1 over minus 6 minus 2 equals 4 minus r over minus 8.

16
00:02:29.166 --> 00:02:35.663
STEP 3 times SET THE PRODUCT OF GRADIENTS EQUAL TO minus 1.

17
00:02:35.823 --> 00:02:49.289
Key rule: PERPENDICULAR LINES. m sub 1 m sub 2 equals minus 1. 4 minus r over 16 equals minus 1, so 4 minus r equals minus 16 and r equals 20.

18
00:02:49.449 --> 00:02:54.957
Perpendicular segments satisfy m sub 1 m sub 2 equals minus 1.

19
00:02:55.117 --> 00:03:05.272
(minus 12)(4 minus r over minus 8) equals 4 minus r over 16 equals minus 1 4 minus r equals minus 16 which gives r equals 20.

20
00:03:05.692 --> 00:03:09.689
STEP 4 times CHECK.

21
00:03:09.849 --> 00:03:22.598
With r equals 20, R equals (minus 6, minus 15), so m sub QR equals minus 15 minus 1 over minus 6 minus 2 equals minus 16 over minus 8 equals 2.

22
00:03:22.758 --> 00:03:31.156
m sub QP m sub QR equals (minus 12)(2) equals minus 1 Pythagoras confirms the right angle.

23
00:03:31.316 --> 00:03:36.813
PQ squared equals (minus 8) squared plus 4 squared equals 80.

24
00:03:36.973 --> 00:03:52.210
QR squared equals (minus 8) squared plus (minus 16) squared equals 320 and PR squared equals 0 squared plus (minus 20) squared equals 400, with 80 plus 320 equals 400.

25
00:03:52.370 --> 00:04:00.945
QP is shallow (gradient minus 12) and QR is steep (gradient 2); the diagram shows the right angle at Q.

26
00:04:01.365 --> 00:04:09.255
So the answer is: (a) R equals (minus 6, 5 minus r) (b) r equals 20.

27
00:04:09.675 --> 00:04:18.589
That completes HKDSE 2026 Paper 1 Question 3. Every step shown here matches the worked solution on the page.
